    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0864" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-29T16:00:00+08:00">November 29,
                            1948—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—7:22 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2356. Our best information confirms our 2355, November 29 that important branches
                    Government will move Canton and certain less important organs to Chungking. No
                    date for removal has been set.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
